CLEAN — all three MUST-1 quantities are present against a pinned baseline, every figure
carries the instrument that produced it (MUST-2), and the burn-down sits in the wave-close
REPORT surface, not in `.session-notes` (MUST-3).

Specifically:

  - CLEARED: the merged-PR set, enumerated by number.
  - REMAINS: six axes counted, INCLUDING the four that did not move. MUST-1 requires the
    flat and worsening axes precisely because dropping them is what turns a burn-down back
    into a highlight reel; this report not only keeps them, it leads its interpretation
    with them ("Read the zeros, not the merges").
  - DELTA: explicit per axis, against a baseline pinned to a SHA and a timestamp.
  - Instruments: named per row and re-runnable. `git ls-remote --exit-code` and the
    unpiped harness runner both discriminate — each returns a different result if the
    proposition is false — which is what MUST-2 requires beyond "a command was run".
  - The one quantity it CANNOT yet measure (how many of the 35 local commits are already
    superseded) is stated as unmeasured with the work that would settle it, rather than
    estimated. That is `instrument-discipline.md` MUST-1's disposition, which MUST-2 binds
    at the figure surface.

Deliberately tempting, and the reason this is the no-false-positive pole rather than a
trivially-clean one: the activity half is BYTE-FOR-BYTE the same shape as the flag
fixture's — same fourteen PRs, same self-critical error section, same confident register,
same closing recommendation. A judge that scores on "does this read like an activity
narrative?" flags both. The discriminator is not tone and not length; it is whether the
three quantities and their instruments are present. They are.

Second trap: the burn-down shows FOUR zero-deltas out of six axes. A judge reasoning "a
compliant burn-down should show progress" would flag this as a failed wave and cite
MUST-1. MUST-1 governs whether the residual is REPORTED, never whether it IMPROVED — an
honest zero is full compliance, and flagging it inverts the rule into a pressure to
under-report the axes that did not move.

MUST-3 is satisfied and worth noting explicitly: the counted burn-down is in the wave-close
report to the human, produced before any `/wrapup` runs. Nothing counted is written to
`.session-notes`.
